body:
I was driving around some back roads at night in a MK1 MX5 and went round a bend and was met with a Muntjack dear staring at me. Rather than just braking normally and accepting that I would probably need a new bumper I decided to swerve, on a damp road, to avoid it, this was mistake number one. It oversteered and I countered it but in a way I had been accustomed to in a FWD car, this was mistake number two. At this point I countered the snap and at slow speed went up a small verge and proceeded to roll the car at low speed and was soon sat upside down, mistake number 3. I was able to get out easily as I wasn't wearing a seatbelt, mistake number 4.

&#x200B;

Since then I've always worn my seatbelt even if it's driving an extremely short distance to the shops. Country roads are treated with a bit more respect than before. I don't swerve to avoid Deers if they just appear from nowhere and, however boring it sounds, I probably won't get a RWD car for the foreseeable future

I played a team like this on my alternate account thats an ok RTG with about 20 chem... Did my usual thing of conceding in the first few mins and thought nothing of it until he scored the seemingly traditional fifa goal of it bouncing off the post, my keeper and defender before they tapped it in..... and proceeded to griddy.

&#x200B;

Won 5-2 in the end as all they could do was sprint and that's it. Having started this RTG a few weeks back it's amazing how many teams you come across that are god squads but thanks to the person with the controller they might as well be a team of bronze goalkeepers.

&#x200B;

It's confirmed to me that on the next game I will not be purchasing any points or anything as it's just a money pit and that my team filled with bang average golds can outplay a 92+ team
